/*Try this out :
- ctrl+alt+d to toggle debug mode
- Set a breakpoint on line "mov ax, 5"
Either click the left column next to that line
or put your cursor on that line and press f9 
- ctrl+alt+c to compile
Always compile before executing
- f5 to execute and stop on the breakpoint
- Add watch variables ax, bx and i in the top-right pane
Click the top-right watch pane with the mouse or press ctrl+alt+2.
Type in "ax" and press enter to watch data.
Do the same for "bx" and "i".
- f10 to step over each instruction
Watch the data change in the top-right watch pane
as you step over each instruction.
Watch column 1 is name, column 2 is value and column 3 is type.
- more info can be found below the main function
*/
main :: () { //Everthing in these curly brackets is in the main function.

	#asm { //Everything in these curly brackets is part of this asm block.
		mov ax, 5;
		add bx, ax, 1;
	}
	//ctrl+shift+g to move from code to asm lines.
	//This declares an integer, which compiles to a mov instruction.
	i : int = 2;

	/*To learn more memory
	load_op memory guides/programming/memory
	*/

	/*To learn about assembly
	load_op assembly guides/programming/assembly
	*/
}

